---
name: Read HarfangLab events from the S3 export
description: |
  Watches the bucket of the HarfangLab S3 export for new objects and returns
  the OCSF events in them. The export writes a new gzip-compressed NDJSON
  object about every minute, named after its creation time in milliseconds,
  plus an empty `test-connection` object that the glob skips.

  `from_s3` keeps no state across restarts and reads every matching object
  again on start. This example therefore moves each object to `processed/`
  after reading it, which keeps the bucket as an archive and needs permission
  to write and delete objects. Alternatives:

  - `remove=true` deletes each object after reading it, if the bucket needs
    no archive.
  - `max_age=10min` skips older objects. This bounds what a restart reads
    again, but objects that arrive while the pipeline is down for longer are
    never read.
  - S3 event notifications to an SQS queue, read with `from_amazon_sqs`,
    deliver each new object once without scanning the bucket.
---

from_s3 "s3://example-bucket/harfanglab/*.json.gz",
  watch=1min,
  rename=(path => f"processed/{path}") {
  decompress_gzip
  read_ndjson
}
